 "geometry": {
  "common": "Soffit 700 wide; vertical 70 mm edge; 30x30 mm inward splay; upper body 640 wide to top (H-100 vertical). Joint keys between adjacent girders are formed by this 30 mm set-back.",
  "hollow_void": "Void 400 wide (120 mm side walls from the 640 face), vertical sides H1 high; top 300 wide with 50x50 chamfers; bottom V 110 high to a centre apex H3 above soffit; top slab H2. Depth chain H = H2+50+H1+110+H3."
 },
 "geometry_notes": [
  "Midspan gross concrete section; strands, stirrups, transverse-tie holes and end solid zones excluded.",
  "Void corners modelled sharp as drawn.",
  "Solid types with the same depth share one outline (e.g. AS05=AS06=BS05=BS06); they are distinct JIS designations (span, strands), kept as separate SIZES following the existing JisTGirderSection precedent. Distinct outlines: 4 solid depths and 14 hollow (H,H1,H2,H3) combinations (18 in total).",
  "Published yuc/ylc are distances from the neutral axis to the top/bottom fibre (ylc negative)."
 ],
